>
  <section class="stack-lg">
    <p class="eyebrow">About the framework</p>
    <h1>Ethotechnics: governance and care infrastructure for high-stakes systems</h1>
    <p class="section-lead">
      Ethotechnics is a framework for designing, evaluating, and governing high-stakes
      socio-technical systems with explicit accountability, burden management, and
      care-infrastructure commitments.
    </p>
    <p>
      The framework is authored by <strong>Kanav Jain</strong>, and developed through
      standards writing, glossary curation, field diagnostics, and implementation-oriented
      research.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-sm card">
    <p class="eyebrow">Institute and Studio</p>
    <h2>How the Institute and Studio fit together</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Ethotechnics Institute (.org)</strong> is the public, open-access commons:
      standards, ontology, glossary, diagnostics, and field notes are free to use,
      cite, and build on.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Ethotechnics Studio (.com)</strong> provides paid clinical AI safety
      evaluations, VC diligence, and governance advisory. The Institute publishes
      the open framework, standards, and self-serve diagnostics.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://ethotechnics.com/studio/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
        Visit Ethotechnics Studio →
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>

